{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And the charge of Elazar son of Aharon the priest: the oil of the lamp and the incense of spices.</b> The Ramban, of blessed memory, wrote that the fact it says 'and the charge of Elazar' and not 'and the burden of Elazar' as it says 'the burden of the sons of Kohath,' indicates from this that Elazar did not carry them but was the officer appointed over them. But from the Yerushalmi we find that Elazar carried them himself, and it was surely a great burden, for the incense alone was 365 maneh, and the oil of the lamp for an entire year was 183 log, and it was without doubt a miraculous occurrence. Thus far the language of the Rav, of blessed memory." "<b>And I found</b> in the Yerushalmi, in the chapter HaMatznin: the oil of the lamp in his right hand, the meal-offering of the incense of spices in his left hand, and the meal-offering of the daily offering of the day suspended from his arm, and the anointing oil in a small flask on his right side suspended from his belt."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The closing phrase 'עד כאן לשון הרב ז״ל' marks the end of Ramban's quoted words; 'הרב' here refers to Ramban, cited at the comment's opening."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:30:24.060104535Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}